{"_id":"q_quiz_ai_0","quiz_id":"quiz_ai","question":"What type of AI learns from labeled training data?","options":["Unsupervised Learning","Reinforcement Learning","Supervised Learning","Transfer Learning"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Supervised learning uses labeled input-output pairs to train models.","order_index":0}
{"_id":"q_quiz_ai_1","quiz_id":"quiz_ai","question":"Which algorithm mimics the human brain?","options":["Decision Tree","Neural Network","K-Means","Linear Regression"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Neural networks are inspired by the structure of the human brain.","order_index":1}
{"_id":"q_quiz_ai_2","quiz_id":"quiz_ai","question":"What does \"overfitting\" mean in ML?","options":["Model too simple","Model performs perfectly","Model memorizes training data, poor generalization","Model trains too fast"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Overfitting = model learns training noise, fails on new data.","order_index":2}
{"_id":"q_quiz_ai_3","quiz_id":"quiz_ai","question":"What is the Turing Test?","options":["CPU benchmark","Test if machine exhibits human-like intelligence","Database query test","Graphics test"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Turing Test (1950): machine passes if it can converse like a human.","order_index":3}
{"_id":"q_quiz_ai_4","quiz_id":"quiz_ai","question":"What is \"gradient descent\" used for?","options":["Data visualization","Minimizing loss during training","Sorting datasets","Loading models"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Gradient descent minimizes the loss function by adjusting model weights.","order_index":4}
{"_id":"q_quiz_dsa_0","quiz_id":"quiz_dsa","question":"What is the time complexity of binary search?","options":["O(n)","O(log n)","O(n²)","O(1)"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Binary search halves the search space each step: O(log n).","order_index":0}
{"_id":"q_quiz_dsa_1","quiz_id":"quiz_dsa","question":"Which data structure follows LIFO?","options":["Queue","Stack","Array","Linked List"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Stack follows LIFO — Last In, First Out.","order_index":1}
{"_id":"q_quiz_dsa_2","quiz_id":"quiz_dsa","question":"Worst-case time complexity of QuickSort?","options":["O(n log n)","O(n)","O(n²)","O(log n)"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"QuickSort is O(n²) worst-case when pivot is always smallest/largest.","order_index":2}
{"_id":"q_quiz_dsa_3","quiz_id":"quiz_dsa","question":"In a BST, where is the smallest element?","options":["Root","Rightmost node","Leftmost node","Last level"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"In a BST, smaller values go left, so the leftmost node is smallest.","order_index":3}
{"_id":"q_quiz_dsa_4","quiz_id":"quiz_dsa","question":"Which traversal visits Left → Root → Right?","options":["Preorder","Inorder","Postorder","Level-order"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Inorder traversal: Left, Root, Right. Gives sorted output for BST.","order_index":4}
{"_id":"q_quiz_python_0","quiz_id":"quiz_python","question":"What is the correct way to define a function in Python?","options":["function myFunc():","def myFunc():","func myFunc():","define myFunc():"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"In Python, functions are defined using the \"def\" keyword.","order_index":0}
{"_id":"q_quiz_python_1","quiz_id":"quiz_python","question":"Which data type is MUTABLE in Python?","options":["String","Tuple","List","Integer"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Lists are mutable — you can change elements after creation.","order_index":1}
{"_id":"q_quiz_python_2","quiz_id":"quiz_python","question":"What does len([1, 2, 3, 4]) return?","options":["3","4","5","Error"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"len() returns the number of items. [1,2,3,4] has 4 elements.","order_index":2}
{"_id":"q_quiz_python_3","quiz_id":"quiz_python","question":"How do you start a comment in Python?","options":["//","#","/*","--"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Python uses the # symbol to start single-line comments.","order_index":3}
{"_id":"q_quiz_python_4","quiz_id":"quiz_python","question":"What is the output of print(type(3.14))?","options":["<class 'int'>","<class 'float'>","<class 'double'>","<class 'number'>"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"3.14 is a float, so type() returns <class float>.","order_index":4}
{"_id":"q_quiz_security_0","quiz_id":"quiz_security","question":"What does SQL injection exploit?","options":["Weak passwords","Unvalidated user input in SQL queries","Slow servers","Outdated browsers"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"SQL injection inserts malicious SQL via unvalidated inputs.","order_index":0}
{"_id":"q_quiz_security_1","quiz_id":"quiz_security","question":"What does HTTPS provide over HTTP?","options":["Faster speeds","Encrypted communication","More features","Better SEO only"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"HTTPS uses TLS/SSL encryption for secure data transfer.","order_index":1}
{"_id":"q_quiz_security_2","quiz_id":"quiz_security","question":"What is a \"zero-day\" vulnerability?","options":["Bug fixed on release","Unknown flaw with no patch","24-hour security window","Midnight code issue"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Zero-day = previously unknown flaw exploited before a patch exists.","order_index":2}
{"_id":"q_quiz_security_3","quiz_id":"quiz_security","question":"Which hashing algorithm is NOT recommended for passwords?","options":["bcrypt","Argon2","MD5","scrypt"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"MD5 is cryptographically broken. Use bcrypt, Argon2, or scrypt.","order_index":3}
{"_id":"q_quiz_security_4","quiz_id":"quiz_security","question":"What is phishing?","options":["Network sniffing","Social engineering to steal credentials","DoS attack","Port scanning"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Phishing tricks users into revealing credentials via fake sites/emails.","order_index":4}
{"_id":"q_quiz_web_0","quiz_id":"quiz_web","question":"Which HTML tag is used for the largest heading?","options":["<h6>","<head>","<h1>","<title>"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"<h1> is the largest heading. Headings go from <h1> to <h6>.","order_index":0}
{"_id":"q_quiz_web_1","quiz_id":"quiz_web","question":"Which CSS property changes text color?","options":["font-color","text-color","color","foreground"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The \"color\" property sets the color of text in CSS.","order_index":1}
{"_id":"q_quiz_web_2","quiz_id":"quiz_web","question":"What does DOM stand for?","options":["Document Object Model","Data Object Manager","Desktop Output Module","Design Object Method"],"correct_index":0,"explanation":"DOM = Document Object Model — HTML as a tree structure.","order_index":2}
{"_id":"q_quiz_web_3","quiz_id":"quiz_web","question":"Which JS method selects an element by ID?","options":["querySelector()","getElement()","getElementById()","selectById()"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"getElementById() returns the element with the specified ID.","order_index":3}
{"_id":"q_quiz_web_4","quiz_id":"quiz_web","question":"What does CSS \"flex: 1\" mean?","options":["Fixed width 1px","Element grows to fill space","Single column","Font size 1rem"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"flex: 1 is shorthand for flex-grow: 1 — element fills available space.","order_index":4}
